    "title": "Star Tracker",
    "summary": "A microcontroller-based motorized star tracker designed to locate and follow celestial objects using equatorial coordinates. The system combines real-time sensor data, time synchronization, and stepper motor control to achieve automated astronomical track",
    "description": "This project involves designing and building a two-stage star tracking system: a prototype and a full-scale motorized telescope mount. The ESP32 collects orientation data from sensors (MPU6050/MPU9250), synchronizes time using NTP, and computes astronomical coordinates such as Right Ascension and Declination. These values are transmitted to an Arduino Mega, which controls stepper motors to physically align the system with target celestial objects. The project integrates concepts from embedded systems, sensor fusion, celestial mechanics, and mechanical design, while addressing challenges like sensor noise, motor torque limitations, and system stability.\r\n\r\nDespite a working prototype, the final implementation faced unresolved challenges and could not be completed within the project timeline.",
    "tech_stack": "micro-controllers, Rapid Prototyping, Coding",
